	AARG!  My level 11 rogue with +1 Excalibur and -12 AC just got wasted
by an ochre jelly--in 2 hits!  The first did 48 points of damage, the next (I
was down to 17 HP now) did 44 points.  Isn't good AC supposed to protect from
damage as well as hit probability?  For such good AC I find such large amounts
of damage to be both irritating and unfair.
	Perhaps in 3.1 there could be an acid resistance intrinsic, or acid-
resistant armor?
	At least I got a good laugh at the end:  my engagement ring turned
out to be a ring of conflict.  Ironic, eh?
